        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While the big issue, the scaling bug, has been fixed, I still think the scaling ratio is a bit too small when in arm scaling mode.\nMy arms in vr max out just before my arms irl do, and the hand consistently detaches at the end of my reach. I've gotten a few other people to confirm that this is still the case in the last couple nights.\nWith scaling by height now an option, imo there's less reason to err on the too small side since there's a good option there, and there's no way aside from user height/playspace tweaks to make it larger.\nIt's still a super subjective thing so I'm actually really curious what's normal here (partially for imscale too).",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
