  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The IK beta introduced a lot more arm pull (where my VR arms is a lot shorter than my IRL arms) for me, on every avatar I have tested so far. \nThis issue might be related to other users' report where their trackers are under the floor, and their arm length shortened. (I also experienced trackers going under the floor.)\n\nLink to post: https://feedback.vrchat.com/vrchat-ik-20/p/feet-under-the-floor\n\nEDIT:\nAfter discussing with Kung on Discord. It is concluded that:\n1. The arm pull is much less severe while T-posing (around 1 inch) than with arms extended forward. (around 2~3 inches)\n2. It might be worth increasing the back and forth range of motion on the shoulders to combat arm pull.",
